{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016DTakxaj2qNZgWZxKop6n8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity system that has grown a substantial R&D-orchestration layer on top. Grounded summary:\n\n**What it is**\n- A **personal productivity / task-management system for J.C. Liechty**, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain Markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing. Core lists: `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files (`domains/academic.md`, `commercial.md`, etc.), plus archive files for cancelled/saved tasks.\n\n**What it does**\n- Ships **`anchor_gui.py`**, a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes task changes straight back to the markdown. It runs **persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`** (not launched by hand).\n- Ships **`anchor.py`**, a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n- Supports a full **task lifecycle** â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” across priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields.\n- Runs a **daily 5 AM health check** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that self-tests file integrity and exercises every endpoint and R&D surface (fully stubbed), writing dated reports.\n\n**What it has become (the R&D \"cockpit\" layer)**\n- Beyond task tracking, Anchor now hosts a multi-generation **R&D control surface** for driving the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** agent trio per project. The current shipped version is **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (merged to master 2026-06-13, with a v4.1 render rebuild).\n- Each project window is a **single-screen cockpit**: lane tiles (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) each with one honest status light, clicking a tile expands an **inline panel** with a session summary over a **real, resizable xterm.js terminal** backed by **ConPTY** sessions.\n- Key cockpit capabilities: **isolated git-worktree sessions** per run, **engine toggle** (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only), a **skill that auto-loads once / greets once** (no repeating-prompt loop), per-lane **doc-role** links, project **cost/tokens/time rollups**, a **grass idea board** (promote to lane), and **type-aware deliverable launch** (skill/tool verify Â· service preview Â· program run Â· doc render).\n\n**Notable constraint it holds itself to**\n- **Python stdlib only**, with exactly **one declared exception**: the optional `pywinpty` (`pip install .[terminal]`), imported lazily in `pty_manager.py` alone for the ConPTY terminals; `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this. No binary formats â€” all files stay accessible from any CLI/editor.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: this is grounded in the project's own docs (CLAUDE.md and the frozen plan anchors), not re-verified against the live code in this turn. If you want, I can spot-check any specific claim (e.g., that v4 is actually merged, or that the stdlib-only rule holds) against the source."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5773f31b-aab5-412c-9c19-b21a86ddd813","uuid":"934e3bc1-8d1f-46e1-8097-fdfb63c3875a","request_id":"req_011Cc2MKg15Ak5i4myUsaeT3"}
